   "html_text": "Lamond’s claim about law’s coerciveness stems from a number of considerations, but undoubtedly one is his understanding of the nature of coercion itself, which was discussed in Section 2.5 above. Whether or not his account of coercion is tenable, what Lamond says about why law is coercive generates independent difficulties. Even if the law claims to authorize the enforcement of its subjects’ duties, it is not clear why the mere claiming of such authorization would suffice to make the claiming co",
